      "message": "refactor(sim): the app holders carry stock as CarriedStock, on either engine\n\ncamcraft-sim gains CarriedStock (Column(Body) | Field(FieldBody)): build,\ncarry, clip, simulate and one read-back onto the column body, so deviate,\ndisplay, volume and bounds stay the column carry's own code on both arms.\nThe app's holders - stock_sim_carry's Held and walk, rest/across's sweep,\nrest's prior_state and PriorPlan - hold Stock / CarriedStock instead of\nDexel / Body. The column engine stays the default, call for call, so every\nshipped verdict, golden and stamp is unchanged; the engine is a per-thread\nchoice (stock_sim::with_carry_engine, CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field).\n\nThe field arm is a closed solid over the stock grid's own lattice (a\nverdict column is a field cell centre). Its clip is the column law as a\nsolid (minus the prism above the entered stock's top), not an\nintersection that would delete what stands beside the new block. A\ncolumn cut through reads the stock's own extent, both ends finite, so the\nverdict convicts it instead of reading air. A cylinder stock is refused\nby name on the field arm (its mesh holds less than the round).\n\nPinned by sim carried_stock (6) and the heavy lane\ncarried_engine_agreement (release, --ignored): 14 documents of the\nsetup_carry, rest_across_setups and carried_verify fixtures read on both\nengines, 0 findings.\n\nRefs #637\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
